* sg13g2-pll :: sim/sg13cmos5l-vco-output-levels (issue #190, spec row 14)
* Open-loop VCO output levels into the row-14 load: a 50 fF capacitor from
* the `vco` CLK pin to ground (spec/target-spec.md row 14: V_OH >= 0.9 x VDD,
* V_OL <= 0.1 x VDD into <= 50 fF, single-ended, rail-referenced).
*
* Settled levels, deliberately conservative: V_OH is the MINIMUM of v(clk)
* over the middle half of one settled high phase, V_OL the MAXIMUM over the
* middle half of one settled low phase.  A plain max/min would credit
* overshoot; this takes the worst point of the plateau.  vmax/vmin over the
* same window are reported as information only.  Phase edges come from the
* 50%-of-rail (1.65 V) crossings, cycles 5 and 6 (the ring start-up is
* skipped, as in sg13cmos5l-vco-duty-cycle).
*
* Placeholders are substituted by testbench/gen_requests.py.  The DUT is
* vco_open.spice: the frozen netlist-snapshots/vco.spice with XCDECAP
* commented out (ideal zero-impedance VDD_VCO/GND_VCO make it inconsequential
* to every node voltage measured; same derivation as the duty-cycle bench).

.lib @PDK_ROOT@/@PDK@/libs.tech/ngspice/models/cornerMOShv.lib @CORNER_MOS@
.lib @PDK_ROOT@/@PDK@/libs.tech/ngspice/models/cornerRES.lib @CORNER_RES@
.option scale=1 temp=@TEMP@
.global sub!

.include vco_open.spice

Vvctrl vctrl 0 dc @VCTRL@
Vb0 b0 0 dc @B0V@
Vb1 b1 0 dc @B1V@
Vdd vdd 0 dc 3.3
Vsub sub! 0 dc 0

Xvco vctrl b0 b1 clk vdd 0 vco
Cload clk 0 50f

.ic v(xvco.ring1)=0.5

.tran @TSTEP@ 25n

.control
run
meas tran rise1 when v(clk)=1.65 rise=5
meas tran fall1 when v(clk)=1.65 fall=5
meas tran rise2 when v(clk)=1.65 rise=6
meas tran fall2 when v(clk)=1.65 fall=6
let th = fall1 - rise1
let tl = rise2 - fall1
let hs = rise1 + 0.25*th
let he = fall1 - 0.25*th
let ls = fall1 + 0.25*tl
let le = rise2 - 0.25*tl
meas tran voh min v(clk) from=$&hs to=$&he
meas tran vol max v(clk) from=$&ls to=$&le
meas tran vmax max v(clk) from=$&rise1 to=$&rise2
meas tran vmin min v(clk) from=$&rise1 to=$&rise2
print rise1 fall1 rise2 fall2 voh vol vmax vmin
.endc
.end
